# Support content — docs to help surfaces

**Non-negotiable:** support content ships with the feature, not after it.

Full checklist: **`support-content`** skill (`.agent/skills/support-content/SKILL.md`). Claude Code / OpenCode: invoke it before claiming material work done.

| Change                                 | Update                                                                                      |
| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Page, section, save flow, validation   | Matching `docs/guides/routes/**` guide + **Host-facing knowledge**                          |
| New page or route                      | New guide from `docs/guides/_template.md` + README row                                      |
| Cross-cutting answer (billing, access) | `docs/guides/support/faqs.md` (category + audience + source)                                |
| Guest / public behavior                | `/support`, `/account/help`, and guest prompt starters when relevant                        |
| Sync / provenance / schema             | Preserve `origin='manual'` rows and `is_published`; prune synced rows by `content_key` only |

## Minimums

- **5+ Q&A** for major module pages (org, property operations, growth, config, parking, guest trips/stays/vouchers/tickets).
- **3+ Q&A** for every other documented guide.
- `admin/**` is exempt and never appears on host surfaces.

## Before claiming done

```bash
bun run check:support-content
bun run check:ai-knowledge-coverage
bun run test:support-content
bun scripts/sync-ai-knowledge-base.ts --dry-run
```

## Copy

Follow **`human-copy`**: short, plain, no em dashes, no AI tells. Use host-facing plan names only (`growth` is **Pro**, `pro` is **Business**). Never mention `business_plus` or `commission`.

